---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";

const pageTitle = "About | May Zin";
const description =
  "About May Zin, a software engineer exploring data engineering, agentic AI and responsible AI-assisted development.";
---

<BaseLayout title={pageTitle} description={description}>
  <article class="about-page">
  <header class="about-hero">
    <p class="eyebrow">ABOUT / FIELD NOTES</p>
    <h1>Engineering, curiosity and continuous learning.</h1>
    <p class="lead">
      A software engineer exploring reliable data systems, responsible
      agentic AI and better ways to learn.
    </p>
  </header>

  <div class="about-sections">
    <section aria-labelledby="who-i-am">
      <div class="section-heading">
  <span class="section-icon" aria-hidden="true">🧭</span>
  <h2 id="who-i-am">Who I Am</h2>
</div>

      <p>
        I have worked as a software engineer for many years. Living and
        working in Singapore—one of Southeast Asia’s major business hubs—has
        given me an environment where I can continue learning and growing
        professionally.
      </p>

      <p>
        Data has become a foundation of modern systems. Organisations collect
        and transform it to generate insights, support decisions and prepare
        trustworthy inputs for AI. At the same time, the AI ecosystem is
        maturing, with greater attention being paid to security, governance
        and access control.
      </p>

      <p>
        Technology moves quickly, and I believe engineers should never stop
        learning. I am especially drawn to experimentation, research and
        unfamiliar problems rather than repetitive work. Curiosity and the
        desire to understand how systems work are what keep me learning.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section aria-labelledby="what-i-work-on">
      <div class="section-heading">
  <span class="section-icon" aria-hidden="true">⚙️</span>
  <h2 id="what-i-work-on">What I Work On</h2>
</div>

      <p>
        I build and maintain business software using C# and SQL, with an
        emphasis on reliable data flows, system integrations and maintainable
        solutions. My current direction extends into data engineering, where I
        explore Azure Data Factory, Synapse, Databricks, Spark and lakehouse
        architecture through hands-on projects.
      </p>

      <p>
        Alongside this, I study agentic AI—not merely how agents call tools,
        but how permissions, human approval, tracing, testing and guardrails
        can make them trustworthy. I am most interested in the point where
        practical engineering and responsible experimentation meet.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section aria-labelledby="how-i-learn">
      <div class="section-heading">
  <span class="section-icon" aria-hidden="true">🧪</span>
  <h2 id="how-i-learn">How I Build and Learn</h2>
</div>

      <p>
        AI assistants can shorten the feedback loop and make unfamiliar
        subjects easier to approach. However, speed is not correctness. I do
        not want to accept suggestions simply because they arrive instantly.
      </p>

      <p>
        I question assumptions, resolve doubts, inspect generated work and
        test it before making a decision. To ask useful questions and judge
        the answers, we still need underlying knowledge. Engineers are not
        becoming extinct; we are evolving into more capable, AI-augmented
        engineers.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section aria-labelledby="beyond-engineering">
      <div class="section-heading">
  <span class="section-icon" aria-hidden="true">📚</span>
  <h2 id="beyond-engineering">Beyond Engineering</h2>
</div>

      <p>
        Beyond my professional work, I am an avid reader who has always
        devoured books. I am drawn to science fiction, non-fiction, culture,
        history, ancient knowledge, horror and thrillers. These different
        worlds continually feed my curiosity and influence the way I think as
        an engineer.
      </p>

      <p>
        I also love travelling to faraway lands shaped by rich cultures, long
        histories and natural beauty. To me, reading and travelling are both
        forms of exploration: they reveal new ways to understand people,
        systems and the world around us.
      </p>
    </section>
  </div>
</article>
</BaseLayout>
<style>
  .about-page {
    display: grid;
    gap: clamp(3rem, 8vw, 6rem);
  }

  .about-hero {
    max-width: 52rem;
    position: relative;
    padding-bottom: 2rem;
  }

  .about-hero::after {
    content: "";
    position: absolute;
    bottom: 0;
    left: 0;
    width: 5rem;
    height: 0.35rem;
    background: var(--colour-playful);
    border-radius: 999px;
  }

  .eyebrow {
    color: var(--colour-primary);
    font-family: "JetBrains Mono", monospace;
    font-size: 0.875rem;
    letter-spacing: 0.08em;
    margin-bottom: 1.25rem;
  }

  .lead {
    max-width: 44rem;
    color: var(--colour-primary);
    font-size: clamp(1.15rem, 2vw, 1.35rem);
    margin-top: 1.5rem;
  }

  .about-sections {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr));
    gap: 1.5rem;
  }

  .about-sections section {
    background: var(--colour-surface);
    border: 1px solid var(--colour-border);
    border-top: 0.4rem solid var(--colour-primary);
    border-radius: 0.75rem;
    box-shadow: 0.35rem 0.35rem 0 var(--colour-border);
    padding: clamp(1.5rem, 4vw, 2.5rem);
  }

  .about-sections section:first-child,
  .about-sections section:last-child {
    grid-column: 1 / -1;
  }

  .about-sections section:nth-child(even) {
    border-top-color: var(--colour-playful);
  }

  .section-heading {
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 0.85rem;
    margin-bottom: 1.25rem;
  }

  .section-heading h2 {
    margin: 0;
  }

  .section-icon {
    display: grid;
    width: 2.75rem;
    height: 2.75rem;
    flex-shrink: 0;
    place-items: center;
    background: var(--colour-background, #f7f4ea);
    border: 1px solid var(--colour-border);
    border-radius: 50%;
    font-size: 1.3rem;
  }

  .about-sections p {
    max-width: 72ch;
  }

  .about-sections p:last-child {
    margin-bottom: 0;
  }

  @media (max-width: 48rem) {
    .about-sections {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    }

    .about-sections section:first-child,
    .about-sections section:last-child {
      grid-column: auto;
    }
  }
</style>